@verbs pager
@tier player
@title reading a long text one screen at a time
@see columns rows

When a text does not fit on your screen, the game shows it in parts
and waits for you to say how to go on. At the bottom you see which
lines you are reading, out of how many, and how much you have read.

Type one of these. The ones with <n> take a number in front, saying
how many times or how far.

  (enter) or f   the next screen; <n>f skips <n> screens
  b              the previous screen; <n>b goes back <n>
  d              half a screen down; <n>d, <n> halves
  u              half a screen up; <n>u, <n> halves
  (space) or z   one more line; <n>z, <n> lines
  .              shows the current screen again
  <n>s           skips <n> lines forward
  <n>g           goes to line <n>
  G              goes to the end; <n>G, to <n> lines from the end
  <n>%           goes to <n> per cent of the text: 50% is the middle
  /<text>        searches forward for the text; / alone repeats the
                 last search
  -<text>        searches backward for the text
  h or ?         this help
  q              stops reading

How many lines fit on each screen is set with rows.
